    "content": "Playbook: {\"playbook_name\": \"Suspicious DNS Query Triage\", \"description\": \"SOP for triaging DNS Tunneling anomalies by normalizing the alert domain to its root (eTLD+1) and performing conditional age checks.\", \"steps\": [{\"step_id\": 1, \"task\": \"Extract DNS Context from Alert\", \"action\": \"Identify the primary domain from the Alert 'description' or 'evidence.sample_queries'.\", \"requirement\": \"STRICTLY use the domain that triggered this specific alert. Do not use domains from the Recent Events list for the primary triage check.\"}, {\"step_id\": 2, \"task\": \"Conditional Root Domain Age Analysis\", \"action\": \"Strip all subdomains to identify the root domain (eTLD+1). IF this root domain is unknown, INVOKE 'get_domain_age' on the root domain ONLY.\", \"tool_integration\": \"get_domain_age\", \"logic\": \"1. **Normalization:** If the alert query is '***.domain.net', run the check ONLY on 'domain.net'.\\n2. **Conditional Trigger:** Skip the API call if the root domain is a globally trusted provider.\\n3. **Risk Profile:** If the root domain is < 30 days old, escalate to High Priority (HP) as it suggests newly created infrastructure for exfiltration.\"}, {\"step_id\": 3, \"task\": \"Base64 Decoding and Payload Inspection\", \"action\": \"Inspect the subdomains in 'sample_queries' for Base64 characteristics. If found, attempt to decode the string.\", \"logic\": \"If the decoded payload reveals system-related strings (e.g., 'C:\\\\Users\\\\', '/etc/passwd', 'hostname', or PowerShell commands), escalate to High Priority (HP) immediately.\"}, {\"step_id\": 4, \"task\": \"Subdomain Pattern and Payload Analysis\", \"action\": \"Analyze 'sample_queries' for structural indicators of legitimate diagnostics\", \"logic\": \"Legitimate diagnostic patterns on a normalized root domain are strong Low Priority (LP) indicators.\"}, {\"step_id\": 5, \"task\": \"Correlate with Historical Host Activity\", \"action\": \"MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'get_recent_events' AND 'get_recent_similar_alerts' to understand host context.\", \"tool_integration\": [\"get_recent_events\", \"get_recent_similar_alerts\"], \"logic\": \"Determine if the host has a history of similar volume spikes or communication with this root domain.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Final Correlation and Triage Decision\", \"action\": \"Evaluate the normalized domain age, decoded payload results, and the endpoint's role.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - The root domain is verified infrastructure.\\n   - AND the subdomains match known patterns (e.g., DNSSEC sentinel).\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - **Decoded payloads contain sensitive host data.**\\n   - OR the root domain is newly registered (< 30 days).\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-10234\", \"alert_name\": \"DNS Tunneling Anomaly\", \"start_time\": \"2026-02-06T09:58:16.000Z\", \"source_ip\": \"192.168.153.249\", \"destination_ip\": \"172.16.40.3\", \"endpoint\": \"srv-prod-infra-01\", \"description\": \"An anomalously large amount (313 Bytes) of tunneled, high-entropy traffic through DNS (domain: sharepoint.com) was observed.\", \"evidence\": {\"workload\": \"Network\", \"application\": \"DNS\", \"query_type\": \"CNAME\", \"actual_bytes\": 313, \"typical_bytes\": 50, \"sample_queries\": [\"9941-v4v6-cdn.glob-zone.dprod.sharepoint.com\", \"102934-v4v6-farm.cluster01.sharepointonline.com.akadns.net\", \"edge-standard-001.msedge.net\", \"prod-relay-af-092.spo-msedge.net\", \"tenant-files-api.sharepoint.com.res.office365.com\", \"storage-blob-v12.dprodmgd.aa-rt.sharepoint.com\", \"ns-priority-1.spo-msedge.net\"]}}"
  }
]

