    "role": "user",
    "content": "Playbook: {\"playbook_name\": \"EDR Anti-Tampering Triage\", \"description\": \"SOP for triaging attempts to disable, bypass, or tamper with security services.\", \"steps\": [{\"step_id\": 1, \"task\": \"Identify the Actor and Source\", \"action\": \"Look at the alert details to find the computer name, the user account running the command, and the specific process used.\", \"logic\": \"Tampering requires high privileges. If the user is a service account or a 'Global Admin', the risk of a full system compromise is extremely high.\"}, {\"step_id\": 2, \"task\": \"Evaluate the Command Intent\", \"action\": \"Analyze the exact command line. Is it specifically targeting a security service or attempting to hide logs?\", \"logic\": \"Legitimate IT maintenance rarely involves stopping the AV service via a manual command line. This behavior is a primary indicator of an active human attacker or a malicious script.\"}, {\"step_id\": 3, \"task\": \"Check for Preceding 'Malware' or 'Exploit' Alerts\", \"action\": \"MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'get_recent_similar_alerts' and 'get_recent_events' for this computer in the 1 hour before the tampering attempt.\", \"tool_integration\": [\"get_recent_similar_alerts\", \"get_recent_events\"], \"logic\": \"Attackers usually run a 'tamper' command *after* a malware detection is blocked, in an attempt to disable the protection before trying to run the malware again.\"}, {\"step_id\": 4, \"task\": \"Investigate the Parent Process (The 'Who called Who')\", \"action\": \"Identify what started the tampering process. Was it a remote management tool, a script, or a suspicious unknown file?\", \"logic\": \"If the parent is a 'Remote Access' tool not used by your IT team, this is a confirmed intrusion (HP).\"}, {\"step_id\": 5, \"task\": \"Verify Remediation Effectiveness\", \"action\": \"Check the 'remediation status'. If it says 'Failed' or 'Partial', the system is currently unprotected.\", \"logic\": \"Even if 'Blocked', the attempt itself proves the attacker has sufficient permissions to issue the command, which is a critical security failure.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Final Triage Classification\", \"action\": \"Assign triage priority (LP or HP) based on whether the action was authorized.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - The command was run by a verified IT Administrator during a documented maintenance window.\\n   - The command is part of a known-good software uninstaller/updater (verified by signer).\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - **Defense Evasion**: Any attempt to stop security services, clear security logs, or disable MFA.\\n   - **Suspicious Actor**: Command run by a non-admin user or a service account that shouldn't be running system commands.\\n   - **Active Intrusion**: The tampering follows a blocked malware alert or originates from a suspicious parent process.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-29905\", \"alert_name\": \"Microsoft Defender: Antivirus Tampering Attempt Prevented\", \"threat_display_name\": \"MpTamperSrvDisableAV\", \"threat_family_name\": \"Defense Evasion / Tampering\", \"status\": \"new\", \"start_time\": \"2025-10-09T15:39:02.000Z\", \"description\": \"An attempt to stop the Microsoft Defender Antivirus service (WinDefend) via the Service Control Manager (sc.exe) was detected and blocked.\", \"alert_web_url\": \"https://security.microsoft.com/alerts/mptamp-stop-windefend-cl202\", \"evidence\": {\"endpoint\": \"WKSTN-FIN-092b\", \"source_ip\": \"10.10.44.112\", \"user\": \"GlobalAdmin_svc\", \"process_name\": \"sc.exe\", \"process_path\": \"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\sc.exe\", \"command_line\": \"C:\\\\windows\\\\system32\\\\sc.exe stop WinDefend\", \"remediation_status\": \"success\", \"remediation_action\": \"remove / blocked\"}}"
  }
]

