    "content": "Playbook: {\"playbook_name\": \"EDR SaaS & Email Identity Triage\", \"description\": \"SOP for triaging identity-based alerts such as suspicious mailbox rules and unauthorized forwarding. Focuses on identifying Account Takeover (ATO) and Business Email Compromise (BEC).\", \"steps\": [{\"step_id\": 1, \"task\": \"Extract Identity & Actor Context\", \"action\": \"Parse alert for user_account, source_ip, affected_mailbox, and rule_details. Identify the account type.\", \"logic\": \"High-value targets (VIPs) or service accounts with global permissions elevate the initial risk.\"}, {\"step_id\": 2, \"task\": \"Analyze Rule Intent\", \"action\": \"Examine the 'logic' of the mailbox rule.\", \"logic\": \"Threat actors use 'Delete' or 'Move to Folder' rules to hide their communication from the actual user and to suppress security notifications.\"}, {\"step_id\": 3, \"task\": \"Cross-Platform Correlation (Lateral Movement)\", \"action\": \"MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'get_recent_events' for the user. Look for 'Impossible Travel' alerts, MFA fatigue attempts, or suspicious logins preceding the rule creation.\", \"tool_integration\": [\"get_recent_events\"], \"logic\": \"A successful login from a new device/location followed immediately by a mailbox rule change is a confirmed Account Takeover.\"}, {\"step_id\": 4, \"task\": \"Impact Assessment\", \"action\": \"Check if the affected entities include external mail-flow. If 'Forwarding' is enabled, identify the destination address.\", \"logic\": \"Data exfiltration via auto-forwarding to a personal or look-alike domain is a critical HP event.\"}, {\"step_id\": 5, \"task\": \"Final Triage Classification\", \"action\": \"Assign triage priority (LP or HP) based on the legitimacy of the access and the impact of the rule.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - Action performed by a known account as part of documented cleanup.\\n   - Geolocation and IP match the user's standard office/VPN profile.\\n   - The rule is a standard 'Move to Folder' for organization.\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - **Stealth Behavior**: Rule deletes or hides incoming mail on a human-user account.\\n   - **Credential Compromise**: Rule was created following an 'Anomalous Login' or 'MFA Bypass'.\\n   - **Exfiltration**: Rule forwards internal email to an external, unauthorized address.\\n   - **Origin**: Action originated from a high-risk IP or unexpected country.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-29490\", \"alert_name\": \"Trend Micro Vision One: Suspicious Mailbox Rule Deletes All Incoming Emails\", \"status\": \"new\", \"start_time\": \"2026-02-17T11:05:17.000Z\", \"description\": \"Trend Micro Vision One reported a suspicious alert with the following details - Threat Name of \\\"Suspicious Mailbox Rule Deletes All Incoming Emails\\\"\", \"evidence\": {\"alert_id\": \"WB-31720-20260208-00003\", \"affected_entities\": [\"email: noreply-alerts@client.ee\"], \"user_account\": \"autoreply\", \"detection_source\": \"trendmicro_visionone\", \"msg_class\": \"trendmicro_visionone_alerts\", \"detection_rule\": \"SC-17\"}}"
  }
]

